  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Bring a medium saucepan of water to the boil for the noodles and peas. Crush or finely chop 2 garlic cloves. Shred the carrot using a julienne peeler or coarsely grate with a box grater. Quarter the tofu pieces. Combine the garlic, teriyaki sauce, 1½ tbs soy sauce and 1 tbs honey (see Make it yours) in a large bowl. Add the tofu and toss to coat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1456612/photos/large/prep_ingredients-2d49b2af128dd6d3652bd76f1d3a62d7.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook noodles and peas: Cook the noodles and peas in the pan of boiling water for 2 mins or until tender. Drain, then rinse under hot water to prevent the noodles from sticking.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1456613/photos/large/soak_noodles-acca1d1a9ef90958ddae0b753785286b.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir-fry tofu: Heat 1 tbs vegetable oil in a medium deep frypan over medium heat. Drain the tofu, reserving the marinade. Stir-fry the tofu for 3-4 mins until golden and warmed through.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1456614/photos/large/stir_fry_chicken-84d97949fb36f0ab5aa0f0a383cb035f.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Finish stir-fry: Add the carrot and reserved marinade to the tofu and stir-fry for 30 secs or until the carrot is just tender and the marinade comes to the boil. Add the noodles and peas and stir-fry for 1 min or until warmed through. Remove the pan from the heat. Taste, then season with pepper.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1456615/photos/large/finish_stir_fry-252416ee18bc7f74bd3dc07e05bf8df5.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Divide the tofu noodle stir-fry among bowls. Scatter over the sesame seeds and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1456616/photos/large/serve_up-c63f4c785908e9132916f90d8b794764.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make it yours: We've suggested this amount of honey for flavour, but if you don't like things too sweet, simply reduce to taste.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1456617/photos/large/make_it_yours-2c7398977ad6e937cf3612f6de5ba9b2.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
